# Migration files must be byte-identical everywhere.
#
# Prisma records a SHA-256 of each migration.sql in _prisma_migrations and
# re-checks it on every `migrate deploy`. A Windows checkout without this rule
# gets CRLF, Vercel gets LF, and the two produce different checksums for the
# same file — so a migration applied from one would be reported as "modified
# after it was applied" by the other, and the deploy fails.
#
# vercel.json runs `prisma migrate deploy` on every build, so that failure would
# block deploys rather than just being noisy.
*.sql text eol=lf
